  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "As someone with chronic pain and fatigue, turning my head frequently can be stressful, and reduce the amount of time I can spend in VR. Whilst the Moveable Menu is a godsend for making it easier to view without looking *down*, I still have to look left-to-right to see parts of the menu. Without the ability to move the menu on its Z-axis *away* from me, this creates additional strain.\n \nLikewise, the MM seems to reset with each open; rather than appear directly in the line of sight, I would like the option to \"pin\" its vertical position, as the default positioning with free look is still slightly too low as well for comfort.\nRecommendations:\n- When holding the MM in free-adjust mode, allow the user to articulate the vertical inputs of the controller holding the menu to adjust its \"view distance\" towards or away from the player.\n- Add a \"Pin\" icon next to the MM movement control, below the menu, which can lock both its vertical position, and its distance from the player.",
